# Object

Namespace: `Axiom.Gameplay`

## Description

Base for the live object/component facade. Instantiate creates one runtime entity from an existing template; Destroy removes an entity subtree. These operations affect Play, not the authored scene.

## Use cases

Spawn a temporary pickup or remove a consumed object.

## Example

The statements below belong inside a `MonoBehaviour` callback. Add the components/resources mentioned in the use case first.

```csharp
var original = GameObject.Find("Pickup");
if (original != null) {
 var clone = Instantiate(original, new Vector3(2, 1, 0), Quaternion.identity);
 Destroy(clone);
}
```

## Compatibility and limitations

Transforms use world position/rotation. localScale writes the runtime scale. Legacy Entity.Transform.Position/Rotation/Scale remain snapshots; lowercase transform properties are live. Generic component lookup covers built-in wrappers and already attached scripts. Instantiate clones one entity using the existing spawn contract; it does not yet clone a hierarchy or start new script instances. SetActive controls runtime hierarchy participation; GetComponentInChildren and GetComponentInParent traverse existing components. Dynamic AddComponent, tags and full Unity object identity semantics remain pending.


## Implemented declarations

```csharp
public partial class Object {
 public static GameObject Instantiate(GameObject original)=>Instantiate(original,original.transform.position,original.transform.rotation);
 public static GameObject Instantiate(GameObject original,Vector3 position,Quaternion rotation){var entity=Context.CloneHierarchy(original.Entity,position,rotation);entity.SetRotation(rotation);return new GameObject(entity);}
 public static void Destroy(GameObject target)=>Context.Destroy(target.Entity);
 public static void Destroy(Component target)=>Context.Remove(target);
}

public partial class Object {
 public static void Destroy(GameObject target,double delay)=>RuntimeLifecycle.DestroyAfter(target,delay);
 public static void Destroy(Component target,double delay)=>RuntimeLifecycle.DestroyAfter(target,delay);
 public static GameObject Instantiate(GameObject original,Transform? parent)=>Instantiate(original,parent,true);
 public static GameObject Instantiate(GameObject original,Transform? parent,bool worldPositionStays){var clone=Instantiate(original);var local=Context.Local(original.Entity);clone.transform.SetParent(parent,true);if(!worldPositionStays)Context.LocalTransform(clone.Entity,local.Position,local.Rotation,local.Scale);return clone;}
 public static T[] FindObjectsByType<T>() where T:Component=>Context.Entities.Keys.Where(Context.IsActive).SelectMany(id=>new GameObject(new Entity(id,Context.Generation)).GetComponents<T>()).ToArray();
 public static T? FindFirstObjectByType<T>() where T:Component=>FindObjectsByType<T>().FirstOrDefault();
}

public partial class Object {
 private Entity? Handle=>this is GameObject go?go.Entity:this is Component c?c.Entity:null;
 public int GetInstanceID()=>Handle is Entity e?HashCode.Combine(e.Id,e.Generation,this is Component c?c.GetType():typeof(GameObject)):System.Runtime.CompilerServices.RuntimeHelpers.GetHashCode(this);
 private static bool Exists(Object? value){if(value==null)return false;if(value.Handle is not Entity e)return true;if(e.Generation!=Context.Generation||!Context.Entities.ContainsKey(e.Id))return false;if(value is Script script)return Context.LiveScripts.Contains(script);if(value is Component c&&Context.ComponentKey(c.GetType()) is string key)return Context.EntityData[e.Id].TryGetProperty(key,out _);return true;}
 public static implicit operator bool(Object? value)=>Exists(value);
}
```

# GameObject

Namespace: `Axiom.Gameplay`

## Description

Create an empty runtime GameObject, retrieve/add compiled components, activate it and query live tags/layers. One script instance per compiled physical path and one built-in storage kind per object are supported. AddComponent supports compiled scripts, box/sphere colliders in 2D/3D, Rigidbody/Rigidbody2D, Camera and AudioListener. Asset-backed AudioSource and Animator require authored configuration and can be cloned. Transform cannot be removed.

## Example

```csharp
var child = new GameObject("Sensor");
child.transform.SetParent(transform, false);
child.transform.localPosition = new Vector3(0, 1, 0);
child.tag = "Sensor";
child.AddComponent<BoxCollider>();
```

## Notes

Object.Instantiate copies the full descendant hierarchy and serialized fields of compiled scripts. Static fields and coroutine state are not duplicated. Runtime edits never persist to the authored project.

## Implemented declarations

```csharp
public sealed partial class GameObject : Object {
 internal Entity Entity {get;}
 internal GameObject(Entity entity){Entity=entity;}
 public string name {get=>Context.Metadata(Entity,"name",Entity.Id);set=>Context.Property(Entity,"name",System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonValue.Create(value));}
 public Transform transform=>new(Entity);
 public bool activeSelf=>Context.ActiveStates.GetValueOrDefault(Entity.Id,true);public bool activeInHierarchy=>Context.IsActive(Entity.Id);public void SetActive(bool active)=>Context.Activate(Entity,active);
 public static GameObject? Find(string name){foreach(var (id,data) in Context.EntityData)if(Context.IsActive(id)&&data.TryGetProperty("name",out var value)&&value.GetString()==name)return new(new Entity(id,Context.Generation));return null;}
 public T? GetComponent<T>() where T:Component=>GetComponents<T>().FirstOrDefault();

}

public sealed partial class GameObject {
 public GameObject(string name="New GameObject"){if(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(name)||name.Length>128)throw new ArgumentException("Invalid object name");Entity=Context.CreateObject(name);}
 public string tag {get=>Context.Metadata(Entity,"runtimeTag","Untagged");set{if(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(value)||value.Length>128)throw new ArgumentException("Invalid tag");Context.Property(Entity,"runtimeTag",JsonValue.Create(value));}}
 public int layer {get=>Context.EntityData[Entity.Id].TryGetProperty("runtimeLayer",out var layer)?layer.GetInt32():0;set{if(value<0||value>31)throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException(nameof(value));Context.Property(Entity,"runtimeLayer",JsonValue.Create(value));if(Context.EntityData[Entity.Id].TryGetProperty("collider",out var c)){var node=JsonNode.Parse(c.GetRawText())!;node["layer"]=1u<<value;Context.Property(Entity,"collider",node);}}}
 public bool CompareTag(string value)=>tag==value;
 public static GameObject[] FindGameObjectsWithTag(string tag)=>Context.Entities.Keys.Where(Context.IsActive).Select(id=>new GameObject(new Entity(id,Context.Generation))).Where(e=>e.tag==tag).ToArray();
 public static GameObject? FindWithTag(string tag)=>FindGameObjectsWithTag(tag).FirstOrDefault();
 public T AddComponent<T>() where T:Component=>Context.AddComponent<T>(Entity);
 public bool TryGetComponent<T>(out T? component) where T:Component {component=GetComponent<T>();return component!=null;}
 public T[] GetComponents<T>() where T:Component {
  _=Context.Read(Entity);var result=new List<Component>{transform};var data=Context.EntityData[Entity.Id];
  var hasCollider=data.TryGetProperty("collider",out var c);var twoD=hasCollider?c.GetProperty("dimension").GetInt32()==2:data.TryGetProperty("runtimePhysicsDimension",out var dim)&&dim.GetInt32()==2;
  if(c.ValueKind==JsonValueKind.Object){var sphere=c.GetProperty("shape").GetString()=="sphere";result.Add(twoD?(sphere?new CircleCollider2D(Entity):new BoxCollider2D(Entity)):(sphere?new SphereCollider(Entity):new BoxCollider(Entity)));}
  if(Context.Bodies.ContainsKey(Entity.Id))result.Add(twoD?new Rigidbody2D(Entity):new Rigidbody(Entity));
  if(Context.Cameras.Contains(Entity.Id))result.Add(new Camera(Entity));if(Context.AudioSources.Contains(Entity.Id))result.Add(new AudioSource(Entity));if(Context.Animators.ContainsKey(Entity.Id))result.Add(new Animator(Entity));if(data.TryGetProperty("audioListener",out _))result.Add(new AudioListener(Entity));
  result.AddRange(Context.LiveScripts.Where(s=>s.Entity.Id==Entity.Id));return result.OfType<T>().ToArray();
 }

 public T? GetComponentInChildren<T>(bool includeInactive=false) where T:Component=>GetComponentsInChildren<T>(includeInactive).FirstOrDefault();
 public T? GetComponentInParent<T>(bool includeInactive=false) where T:Component=>GetComponentsInParent<T>(includeInactive).FirstOrDefault();
 public T[] GetComponentsInChildren<T>(bool includeInactive=false) where T:Component {var found=new List<T>();void Visit(Transform node){if(includeInactive||node.gameObject.activeInHierarchy)found.AddRange(node.GetComponents<T>());for(var i=0;i<node.childCount;i++)Visit(node.GetChild(i));}Visit(transform);return found.ToArray();}
 public T[] GetComponentsInParent<T>(bool includeInactive=false) where T:Component {var found=new List<T>();for(Transform? node=transform;node!=null;node=node.parent)if(includeInactive||node.gameObject.activeInHierarchy)found.AddRange(node.GetComponents<T>());return found.ToArray();}
}
```

# Component

Namespace: `Axiom.Gameplay`

## Description

Base for script and built-in component wrappers. Entity identifies its owner; gameObject and transform expose the owner facade. Component searches walk the current runtime hierarchy.

## Use cases

Retrieve the owning Rigidbody without copying scene JSON or inventing entity IDs.

## Example

The statements below belong inside a `MonoBehaviour` callback. Add the components/resources mentioned in the use case first.

```csharp
var body = GetComponent<Rigidbody>();
if (body != null) body.linearVelocity = Vector3.up * 3;
var camera = GetComponentInChildren<Camera>();
if (camera != null) Debug.Log(camera.gameObject.name);
```

## Compatibility and limitations

Transforms use world position/rotation. localScale writes the runtime scale. Legacy Entity.Transform.Position/Rotation/Scale remain snapshots; lowercase transform properties are live. Generic component lookup covers built-in wrappers and already attached scripts. Instantiate clones one entity using the existing spawn contract; it does not yet clone a hierarchy or start new script instances. SetActive controls runtime hierarchy participation; GetComponentInChildren and GetComponentInParent traverse existing components. Dynamic AddComponent, tags and full Unity object identity semantics remain pending.


## Implemented declarations

```csharp
public partial class Component : Object {
 public Entity Entity {get;internal set;}
 public GameObject gameObject=>new(Entity);
 public Transform transform=>new(Entity);
 public T? GetComponent<T>() where T:Component=>gameObject.GetComponent<T>();
 public T? GetComponentInChildren<T>() where T:Component {var own=GetComponent<T>();if(own!=null)return own;for(var i=0;i<transform.childCount;i++){var found=transform.GetChild(i).GetComponentInChildren<T>();if(found!=null)return found;}return null;}
 public T? GetComponentInParent<T>() where T:Component {Transform? current=transform;while(current!=null){var component=current.GetComponent<T>();if(component!=null)return component;current=current.parent;}return null;}
 public bool TryGetComponent<T>(out T? component) where T:Component {component=GetComponent<T>();return component!=null;}
}

public partial class Component {
 public string name {get=>gameObject.name;set=>gameObject.name=value;}
 public string tag {get=>gameObject.tag;set=>gameObject.tag=value;}
 public bool CompareTag(string value)=>gameObject.CompareTag(value);
 public T[] GetComponents<T>() where T:Component=>gameObject.GetComponents<T>();
 public T[] GetComponentsInChildren<T>(bool includeInactive=false) where T:Component=>gameObject.GetComponentsInChildren<T>(includeInactive);
 public T[] GetComponentsInParent<T>(bool includeInactive=false) where T:Component=>gameObject.GetComponentsInParent<T>(includeInactive);
}
```

# Transform

Namespace: `Axiom.Gameplay`

## Description

Live spatial component for world position, quaternion rotation and scale. Lowercase properties read current runtime state and enqueue validated writes. Uppercase Position/Rotation/Scale preserve legacy snapshot access.

## Use cases

Position a spawned entity, orient a character, or derive movement axes.

## Example

The statements below belong inside a `MonoBehaviour` callback. Add the components/resources mentioned in the use case first.

```csharp
transform.position = new Vector3(2, 1, 0);
transform.rotation = Quaternion.Euler(0, 90, 0);
transform.localScale = Vector3.one * 2;
var facing = transform.forward;
Debug.Log(facing);
```

## Compatibility and limitations

Transforms use world position/rotation. localScale writes the runtime scale. Legacy Entity.Transform.Position/Rotation/Scale remain snapshots; lowercase transform properties are live. Generic component lookup covers built-in wrappers and already attached scripts. Instantiate clones one entity using the existing spawn contract; it does not yet clone a hierarchy or start new script instances. SetActive controls runtime hierarchy participation; GetComponentInChildren and GetComponentInParent traverse existing components. Dynamic AddComponent, tags and full Unity object identity semantics remain pending.


## Implemented declarations

```csharp
public sealed partial class Transform {
 internal Transform(Entity entity){Entity=entity;var v=Context.Read(entity);Position=v.Position;Rotation=v.Rotation;Scale=v.Scale;}
 public Vector3 position {get=>Entity.Transform.Position;set=>Entity.SetPosition(value);}
 public Quaternion rotation {get=>Entity.Transform.Rotation;set=>Entity.SetRotation(value);}
 public Vector3 localScale {get=>Context.Local(Entity).Scale;set=>Context.LocalTransform(Entity,scale:value);}
 public Vector3 localPosition {get=>Context.Local(Entity).Position;set=>Context.LocalTransform(Entity,position:value);}
 public Quaternion localRotation {get=>Context.Local(Entity).Rotation;set=>Context.LocalTransform(Entity,rotation:value);}
 public Vector3 lossyScale=>Entity.Transform.Scale;
 public Vector3 forward=>rotation*Vector3.forward;
 public Vector3 right=>rotation*Vector3.right;
 public Vector3 up=>rotation*Vector3.up;
 public Transform? parent {get=>Context.Parents.GetValueOrDefault(Entity.Id) is string id?new(new Entity(id,Context.Generation)):null;set=>SetParent(value);}
 public void SetParent(Transform? value,bool worldPositionStays=true)=>Context.Parent(Entity,value,worldPositionStays);
 public int childCount=>Context.Parents.Count(p=>p.Value==Entity.Id);
 public Transform GetChild(int index)=>new(new Entity(Context.Parents.Where(p=>p.Value==Entity.Id).ElementAt(index).Key,Context.Generation));
 public Transform? Find(string path){var current=this;foreach(var part in path.Split('/')){Transform? found=null;for(var i=0;i<current.childCount;i++){var child=current.GetChild(i);if(child.gameObject.name==part){found=child;break;}}if(found==null)return null;current=found;}return current;}
 public void Translate(Vector3 translation)=>position+=rotation*translation;
 public void Rotate(double x,double y,double z)=>rotation=rotation*Quaternion.Euler(x,y,z);
 public Vector3 TransformDirection(Vector3 direction)=>rotation*direction;
 public Vector3 InverseTransformDirection(Vector3 direction)=>Quaternion.Inverse(rotation)*direction;
}

public sealed partial class Transform {
 public Transform root {get{var current=this;while(current.parent!=null)current=current.parent;return current;}}
 public bool IsChildOf(Transform other){for(Transform? t=this;t!=null;t=t.parent)if(t.Entity==other.Entity)return true;return false;}
 public Vector3 TransformPoint(Vector3 point)=>position+rotation*new Vector3(point.X*lossyScale.X,point.Y*lossyScale.Y,point.Z*lossyScale.Z);
 public Vector3 InverseTransformPoint(Vector3 point){var p=Quaternion.Inverse(rotation)*(point-position);var s=lossyScale;if(Math.Abs(s.X*s.Y*s.Z)<1e-20)throw new InvalidOperationException("Cannot invert zero scale");return new(p.X/s.X,p.Y/s.Y,p.Z/s.Z);}
 public Vector3 TransformVector(Vector3 vector)=>rotation*new Vector3(vector.X*lossyScale.X,vector.Y*lossyScale.Y,vector.Z*lossyScale.Z);
 public Vector3 InverseTransformVector(Vector3 vector){var p=Quaternion.Inverse(rotation)*vector;var s=lossyScale;return new(p.X/s.X,p.Y/s.Y,p.Z/s.Z);}
 public void SetPositionAndRotation(Vector3 position,Quaternion rotation){this.position=position;this.rotation=rotation;}
 public void SetLocalPositionAndRotation(Vector3 position,Quaternion rotation)=>Context.LocalTransform(Entity,position,rotation);
 public void Translate(Vector3 translation,Space relativeTo){if(relativeTo==Space.World)position+=translation;else Translate(translation);}
 public void Rotate(Vector3 eulers,Space relativeTo=Space.Self){var q=Quaternion.Euler(eulers);rotation=relativeTo==Space.Self?rotation*q:q*rotation;}
}

public sealed partial class Transform {
 public int GetSiblingIndex(){var siblings=Context.Parents.Where(p=>p.Value==Context.Parents.GetValueOrDefault(Entity.Id)).Select(p=>p.Key).ToList();return siblings.IndexOf(Entity.Id);}
 public void SetSiblingIndex(int index){var parent=Context.Parents.GetValueOrDefault(Entity.Id);var siblings=Context.Parents.Where(p=>p.Value==parent).Select(p=>p.Key).ToList();siblings.Remove(Entity.Id);siblings.Insert(Math.Clamp(index,0,siblings.Count),Entity.Id);var entries=Context.Parents.ToArray();Context.Parents.Clear();var queue=new Queue<string>(siblings);foreach(var entry in entries)if(entry.Value==parent){var id=queue.Dequeue();Context.Parents[id]=parent;}else Context.Parents[entry.Key]=entry.Value;Context.Sibling(Entity,index);}
 public void SetAsFirstSibling()=>SetSiblingIndex(0);
 public void SetAsLastSibling()=>SetSiblingIndex(int.MaxValue);
 public void DetachChildren(){foreach(var id in Context.Parents.Where(p=>p.Value==Entity.Id).Select(p=>p.Key).ToArray())new Transform(new Entity(id,Context.Generation)).SetParent(null);}
}

public sealed partial class Transform : Component {
 public Vector3 Position {get;init;}
 public Quaternion Rotation {get;init;}
 public Vector3 Scale {get;init;}
 public Transform(Vector3 position, Quaternion rotation, Vector3 scale) {Position=position;Rotation=rotation;Scale=scale;}
 internal static Transform Read(JsonElement value)=>new(Vector3.Read(value.GetProperty("position")), Quaternion.Read(value.GetProperty("rotation")), Vector3.Read(value.GetProperty("scale")));
}
```

# Entity

Namespace: `Axiom.Gameplay`

## Description

Generation-scoped runtime handle. Legacy methods move, rotate, spawn and control existing physical, audio and animation components. Handles from an earlier Play generation are invalid.

## Use cases

Maintain existing Axiom scripts or write explicitly validated snapshot-based movement.

## Example

The statements below belong inside a `MonoBehaviour` callback. Add the components/resources mentioned in the use case first.

```csharp
var position = Entity.Transform.Position;
Entity.SetPosition(position + Vector3.up);
Debug.Log(Entity.Id);
```

## Compatibility and limitations

Transforms use world position/rotation. localScale writes the runtime scale. Legacy Entity.Transform.Position/Rotation/Scale remain snapshots; lowercase transform properties are live. Generic component lookup covers built-in wrappers and already attached scripts. Instantiate clones one entity using the existing spawn contract; it does not yet clone a hierarchy or start new script instances. SetActive controls runtime hierarchy participation; GetComponentInChildren and GetComponentInParent traverse existing components. Dynamic AddComponent, tags and full Unity object identity semantics remain pending.


## Implemented declarations

```csharp
public readonly record struct Entity(string Id, int Generation) {
 public Transform Transform => Context.Read(this);
 public RigidBody RigidBody => Context.ReadBody(this);
 public void SetVelocity(Vec3 velocity) => Context.Velocity(this,velocity);
 public void Move(Vec3 delta) => SetPosition(Transform.Position+(Vector3)delta);
 public void SetPosition(Vec3 position) => Context.Move(this,position);
 public void SetRotation(Quaternion rotation) => Context.Rotate(this,rotation);
 public bool IsGrounded => Context.Grounded.Contains(Id);
 public Entity FindChildWithCamera() => Context.FindCamera(this);
 public string? CurrentAnimation => Context.AnimationState(this,"currentAnimation");
 public string? WhyAnimationNotPlaying => Context.AnimationState(this,"whyAnimationNotPlaying");
 public void SetAnimationParameter(string name,double value) => Context.Animate(this,"parameter",name,value,0);
 public void PlayAnimation(string state,double crossfadeSeconds=0.3) => Context.Animate(this,"state",state,0,crossfadeSeconds);
 public void PauseAnimation() => Context.Animate(this,"pause",null,0,0);
 public void ResumeAnimation() => Context.Animate(this,"resume",null,0,0);
 public void PlayAudio() => Context.Audio(this,"play",0);
 public void PauseAudio() => Context.Audio(this,"pause",0);
 public void ResumeAudio() => Context.Audio(this,"resume",0);
 public void StopAudio() => Context.Audio(this,"stop",0);
 public void SetAudioVolume(double volume) => Context.Audio(this,"volume",volume);
 public Entity Spawn(Vec3 position) => Context.Spawn(this,position);
}
```

# MonoBehaviour

Namespace: `Axiom.Gameplay`

## Description

Attachable compiled script with enabled/isActiveAndEnabled, ordered lifecycle callbacks, native fixed-step and contact callbacks, coroutines and scheduled methods. Use public override callbacks in Axiom. Disabled behaviours skip updates; their coroutines continue until explicitly stopped, object deactivation, destruction or Stop.

## Example

```csharp
using Axiom.Gameplay;
using System.Collections;
public sealed class Pulse : MonoBehaviour {
    public override void Start() { StartCoroutine(Loop()); }
    private IEnumerator Loop() {
        while (true) { yield return new WaitForSeconds(1); Debug.Log("pulse"); }
    }
}
```

Limits: 256 active coroutines, 256 pending invocations, 32 nested enumerators and 128 immediate advances per resume. A bad callback/yield fails visibly; unsupported yields are never treated as successful asynchronous work.

## Implemented declarations

```csharp
public abstract partial class MonoBehaviour : Script {
 public virtual void OnCollisionEnter(Collision collision){}public virtual void OnCollisionStay(Collision collision){}public virtual void OnCollisionExit(Collision collision){}
 public virtual void OnTriggerEnter(Collider other){}public virtual void OnTriggerStay(Collider other){}public virtual void OnTriggerExit(Collider other){}
 public virtual void OnCollisionEnter2D(Collision2D collision){}public virtual void OnCollisionStay2D(Collision2D collision){}public virtual void OnCollisionExit2D(Collision2D collision){}
 public virtual void OnTriggerEnter2D(Collider2D other){}public virtual void OnTriggerStay2D(Collider2D other){}public virtual void OnTriggerExit2D(Collider2D other){}
 public virtual void Awake(){}public virtual void OnEnable(){}public virtual void Start(){}public virtual void Update(){}public virtual void FixedUpdate(){}public virtual void LateUpdate(){}public virtual void OnDisable(){}public virtual void OnDestroy(){}
 public override void OnStart(){}
 public override void OnUpdate(double deltaSeconds){Update();}
 public override void OnStop(){}
}

public abstract partial class MonoBehaviour {
 public Coroutine StartCoroutine(IEnumerator routine)=>RuntimeLifecycle.Start(this,routine);
 public void StopCoroutine(Coroutine coroutine){if(coroutine.Owner!=this)throw new ArgumentException("Coroutine belongs to another behaviour");RuntimeLifecycle.Stop(coroutine);}
 public void StopCoroutine(IEnumerator routine)=>RuntimeLifecycle.Stop(this,routine);
 public void StopAllCoroutines()=>RuntimeLifecycle.StopAll(this);
 public void Invoke(string methodName,double time)=>RuntimeLifecycle.Invoke(this,methodName,time,0);
 public void InvokeRepeating(string methodName,double time,double repeatRate){if(repeatRate<=0)throw new ArgumentException("Repeat rate must be positive");RuntimeLifecycle.Invoke(this,methodName,time,repeatRate);}
 public void CancelInvoke()=>RuntimeLifecycle.Cancel(this,null);
 public void CancelInvoke(string methodName)=>RuntimeLifecycle.Cancel(this,methodName);
 public bool IsInvoking()=>RuntimeLifecycle.IsInvoking(this,null);
 public bool IsInvoking(string methodName)=>RuntimeLifecycle.IsInvoking(this,methodName);
}
```

# Script

Namespace: `Axiom.Gameplay`

## Description

Script belongs to the script lifecycle API family. Consult the declarations below for the exact supported surface.

## Use cases

Frame-based behaviour.

## Example

```csharp
using Axiom.Gameplay;
public sealed class Motion : MonoBehaviour {
 public double Speed = 1;
 public override void Update() {
  transform.position += Vector3.right * Speed * Time.deltaTime;
 }
}
```

## Compatibility and limitations

Override public callbacks; Unity-style private message methods are not reflected. Existing OnStart/OnUpdate/OnStop overrides remain supported and take precedence if they do not call base. FixedUpdate uses a local 0.02-second accumulator and is not yet a solver-owned callback. LateUpdate follows Update for each behaviour, not a separate global phase. Time uses doubles. Coroutines, Invoke, timeScale and scene loading remain pending.


## Implemented declarations

```csharp
public abstract class Script : Behaviour {
 public virtual void OnStart() {}
 public virtual void OnUpdate(double deltaSeconds) {}
 public virtual void OnStop() {}
}
```

# Time

Namespace: `Axiom.Gameplay`

## Description

Scaled/unscaled delta and elapsed time, frame count, fixed time, inFixedTimeStep and validated timeScale. The fixed solver period is read-only 1/60 second; maximum variable delta is .25 seconds and native catch-up is capped at eight fixed steps. Time resets at Play. realtimeSinceStartup currently means unscaled time since this Play, not process uptime.

## Example

```csharp
public override void Update() {
    if (Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.Space)) Time.timeScale = Time.timeScale == 0 ? 1 : 0;
    transform.position += Vector3.right * Time.deltaTime;
}
```

At timeScale zero Update still runs and unscaled time advances, allowing scripts to unpause. FixedUpdate and scaled timers do not advance.

## Implemented declarations

```csharp
public static class Time {
 private static double scale=1,delta,elapsed,unscaledElapsed,unscaledDelta;
 public static double deltaTime {get=>inFixedTimeStep?fixedDeltaTime:delta;internal set=>delta=value;}
 public static double unscaledDeltaTime {get=>inFixedTimeStep?fixedUnscaledDeltaTime:unscaledDelta;internal set=>unscaledDelta=value;}
 public static double time {get=>inFixedTimeStep?fixedTime:elapsed;internal set=>elapsed=value;}
 public static double unscaledTime {get=>inFixedTimeStep?fixedUnscaledTime:unscaledElapsed;internal set=>unscaledElapsed=value;}
 public static double realtimeSinceStartup=>unscaledTime;
 public static double timeSinceLevelLoad=>time;
 public static double timeAsDouble=>time;
 public static double unscaledTimeAsDouble=>unscaledTime;
 public static double fixedTime {get;internal set;}
 public static double fixedUnscaledTime {get;internal set;}
 public static double fixedUnscaledDeltaTime=>scale>0?fixedDeltaTime/scale:0;
 public static bool inFixedTimeStep {get;internal set;}
 public static double timeScale {get=>scale;set{if(!double.IsFinite(value)||value<0||value>8)throw new ArgumentException("Time scale must be between 0 and 8");scale=value;}}
 public static int frameCount {get;internal set;}
 public const double fixedDeltaTime=1.0/60.0;
 public const double maximumDeltaTime=0.25;
 internal static void Reset(){scale=1;delta=0;time=0;unscaledTime=0;unscaledDeltaTime=0;fixedTime=0;fixedUnscaledTime=0;frameCount=0;inFixedTimeStep=false;}
 internal static void Step(double value){unscaledDeltaTime=value;unscaledTime+=value;delta=Math.Min(value*scale,maximumDeltaTime);time+=delta;frameCount++;}
}
```

# Vector2

Namespace: `Axiom.Gameplay`

## Description

2-component floating vector using doubles. Supports arithmetic, normalization, magnitude, dot product and interpolation. Lowercase aliases coexist with legacy PascalCase fields.

## Use cases

Represent positions, directions, velocities or packed numeric parameters.

## Example

The statements below belong inside a `MonoBehaviour` callback. Add the components/resources mentioned in the use case first.

```csharp
var value = new Vector2(1, 2);
Debug.Log(value.magnitude);
Debug.Log(value.normalized);
```

## Compatibility and limitations

Existing PascalCase names remain supported. Lowercase vector fields and constants are available. Vector numbers use double rather than Unity float. Vector4Int is an Axiom extension. Legacy Vector3.Forward points toward -Z; the Unity-compatible lowercase Vector3.forward points +Z. Axiom cameras look along local -Z. Random wraps the deterministic replay generator; qualify Axiom.Gameplay.Random when System.Random is also in scope. Not every Unity math member is implemented.


## Implemented declarations

```csharp
public record struct Vector2(double X, double Y) {
 public double x {get=>X;set=>X=value;}
 public double y {get=>Y;set=>Y=value;}
 public static Vector2 zero=>Zero;public static Vector2 one=>One;public double magnitude=>Magnitude;public double sqrMagnitude=>X*X+Y*Y;
